# DRAFT - Software-level commands.json vs PF9 path gate

id:                     DRAFT-software-level-commands-json-vs-pf9
trigger_tool:           preflight|ohc-run|gitcode_pr create-pr
phase:                  delivery
error_signature:        PF9 分支/路径闸: 变更路径缺版本目录层|变更路径缺版本目录层.*commands\.json

severity:               2
category:               ohos, conan, ci-gate, metadata, commands-json
match_keywords:         commands.json, PF9, PF8, L0k, E424, R38, software-level, version-level, preflight, no-preflight, CLI tool, bindirs
title:                  CLI packages need a software-level commands.json, which the local PF9 gate rejects

root_cause:             CI's L0k (ci/conan/build_and_test.sh) computes PKG_SOFTWARE_DIR as the parent of the version directory and looks for ${PKG_SOFTWARE_DIR}/commands.json, i.e. archives/<letter>/<package>/commands.json, so a CLI package must put commands.json at the software level. Knowledge entry E424 states the same ("keep it in the software-level directory, not the version directory"), and the repo has 3156 software-level instances versus only 16 version-level ones. However the local gate scripts/ohc/preflight.py PF9 flags any changed archives/ path with fewer than 5 segments as "missing the version directory layer", so every software-level commands.json inevitably trips it.
affected_scope:         Any PR that adds a CLI/application or bindirs-bearing Conan package under archives/<letter>/<package>/ and therefore must ship a software-level commands.json.
verification_cmd:       S=$(git log --diff-filter=A --format=%H -1 origin/main -- archives/l/lsd2/commands.json); python3 scripts/ohc/preflight.py . "${S}^" "$S"

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           keep-software-level-and-treat-pf9-as-known-false-positive
rec_description:        Keep commands.json at the software level (archives/<letter>/<package>/commands.json) to satisfy CI L0k and E424. When creating the PR, treat the PF9 finding for that single path as a known false positive: pass --no-preflight explicitly or state it in the PR description. Verify the false positive by running preflight against an already-merged commit that added a software-level commands.json (e.g. lsd2) and observing the identical finding.
rec_command:            S=$(git log --diff-filter=A --format=%H -1 origin/main -- archives/l/lsd2/commands.json); python3 scripts/ohc/preflight.py . "${S}^" "$S"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      patch-preflight-to-exempt-software-level-commands-json
fallback_description:   Fix the gate itself: in check_branch_and_paths, exempt archives/<letter>/<package>/commands.json (exactly 4 segments, basename commands.json) from the "< 5 segments" check, since PF8 and CI L0k mandate that location. This removes the false positive for all 3156 existing instances.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          repo-script

forbid_1_pattern:       move.*commands\.json.*to.*version|archives/[a-z0-9]/[^/]+/[^/]+/commands\.json
forbid_1_reason:        Relocating commands.json into the version directory silences PF9 but breaks CI L0k, which only reads the software-level path, and contradicts E424.
forbid_1_consequence:   L0k fails ("CLI tool detected but commands.json missing"), so the package cannot land, and PF8 then reports the CLI package as missing its commands.json.
forbid_2_pattern:       duplicate.*commands\.json.*both.*levels
forbid_2_reason:        Keeping two copies does not satisfy PF9 (the software-level one still has 4 segments) and adds a redundant metadata file.
forbid_2_consequence:   No gate passes, and the duplicated metadata can drift out of sync.

principles:             P010,P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
